{#
    The admin screen's own rules — only the athletics-site rows need any.

    🚨 Every colour is a `--c-*` custom property. Convoro's prefix is `--c-`,
    not the `--i-` an IPS habit reaches for, and a wrong prefix paints nothing,
    which on a dark theme reads as white text on white.

    Rows rather than a table, because each one is a form and a `<form>` inside a
    `<tr>` is lifted straight back out by the parser. See index.cvr.
#}
<style>
    .alm-site-row {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: .5rem;
        padding: .45rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
    }

    /* Wide enough that the longest school name does not wrap the row. */
    .alm-site-school {
        flex: 0 0 12rem;
        color: var(--c-text);
        font-weight: 600;
    }

    .alm-site-sport {
        width: 5.5rem;
    }

    /* Pushed right, so the eye runs down one column of states. */
    .alm-site-state {
        flex: 1 1 10rem;
        color: var(--c-text-muted);
        font-size: .85rem;
    }
</style>
